0,Sanskrit - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanskrit,Sanskrit is a classical language belonging to the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European languages. It arose in South Asia after its predecessor languages had diffused there from the northwest in the late Bronze Age.,Sanskrit,Indo-European
1,Sanskrit: the Distant Relative of English,https://www.ba-bamail.com/baba-recommends/sanskrit-the-distant-relative-of-the-english-language/,"Sanskrit is an ancient Indian language, but most people don't know that this archaic language and English have a common ancestor.",Sanskrit,Indo-European
