3,"Indo-European languages | Family, Map, Characteristics... | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Indo-European-languages,"Indo-European languages are a family of languages spoken in most of Europe and areas of European settlement and in much of Southwest and South Asia. The 10 main branches of the family are Anatolian, Indo-Iranian, Greek, Italic, Germanic, Armenian, Tocharian, Celtic...",Sanskrit,Indo-European
4,historical linguistics - Is Sanskrit really the mother of all languages?,https://linguistics.stackexchange.com/questions/32365/is-sanskrit-really-the-mother-of-all-languages,"Sanskrit is an Indo-European (sometimes called Indogermanic ) language, which makes it a relative of English, Spanish, Russian, and many others. But Sanskrit isn't the ancestor of those languages, any more than the composers of the Vedas were the ancestors of all modern Europeans.",Sanskrit,Indo-European
5,Indo-European Studies: Sanskrit | Azam Gill,https://writegill.com/category/indo-european-studies-sanskrit/,"Their language was Sanskrit, a descendent of Brahmi, itself descended from Proto Indo-European (PIO). The most popular hypothesis for the origin of Proto Indo European is that of Robert Renfrew, who locates it in eastern Anatolia around 5000 BC.",Sanskrit,Indo-European
