7,Sanskrit & Armenian: Mothers of ALL Indo-European Languages?,https://thepolyglotfiles.com/2017/05/19/sanskrit-armenian-mothers-of-all-indo-european-languages/,"Further, Sanskrit is an Indo-European language, part of the Indo-Aryan Languages branch, relating it to other languages like Gujarati and Hindi. Sanskrit is a highly inflected language: it has three grammatical genders, three numbers, and eight cases.",Sanskrit,Indo-European
